<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Eurymedon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 466 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Greco-Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Eurymedon was a double victory won around 466 BCE by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimon">Cimon</a> over the Persian Empire at the mouth of the Eurymedon river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamphylia">Pamphylia</a>. Cimon destroyed a Phoenician fleet and then defeated the Persian army on land the same day. The victory ended the Persian naval threat to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> for years and strengthened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>' hold over the league.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-eurymedon.jpg" alt="Battle of the Eurymedon" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adam Franco · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eurymedon_Bridge,_Aspendos,_Turkey._Pic_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
